{"t": 1794113114.7358906, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found and patched in reports/export.py.\n\nCause: upstream ledger 2026.11 added `currency` to every row. export.py's csv.DictWriter only allowed id,amount, so every export raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` (4,120 occurrences in CloudWatch /ecs/reports-api, eu-west-1). That unhandled exception is behind the 502s.\n\nFix: export now writes id,amount,currency and ignores unknown extra fields so future schema drift can't break it. Verified locally with new, legacy, and extra-field rows.\n\nAction needed: deploy/restart the reports-api ECS service (I don't have deploy access from here). Downstream CSV consumers will see the new `currency` header column \u2014 please confirm their parsers handle it."}, "ok": true}
